    "label": "30",
    "prompt": "Solve the following equation.\n$$3x-\\frac{2}{x}=4.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=\\frac{2\\pm\\sqrt{10}}{3}$.",
      "worked": "$x\\ne0$. Multiply by $x$, then use the quadratic formula.\n$$\\begin{align*}3x^2-2&=4x\\\\3x^2-4x-2&=0\\\\x&=\\frac{-(-4)\\pm\\sqrt{(-4)^2-4(3)(-2)}}{2(3)}\\\\x&=\\frac{4\\pm\\sqrt{40}}6\\\\x&=\\frac{2\\pm\\sqrt{10}}3.\\end{align*}$$\nNeither value is zero.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
